<p>Cuba&#x27;s national power grid collapsed again on March 21, triggering another island-wide blackout less than a week after the previous nationwide outage. It was the third major grid failure on the island this month. Cuban authorities called it a &quot;total disconnection&quot; of the national electricity system and said restoration work began soon after the failure. Reports link the repeated outages to a deepening energy crisis driven by aging, deteriorating electricity infrastructure, fuel shortages, and what several outlets describe as a US-imposed oil blockade that has further limited Cuba&#x27;s access to fuel for power generation. In Havana, streets went dark and residents navigated by flashlight, a stark sign of how disruptive the blackout has been to daily life. Humanitarian groups also began sending aid, including solar panels, food and medicine.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/8VHz3zoNL2mGbBf0LMQ7A6hMfY8E6tgHrUHNtNdLLiE2wtPz5jDsjxsdMRLBspAYmhW8o-jLF_96468zzQyZzl_dJJhqwwksRQ5zr7CzON2C5SanqULJq8omITydCvqGXJghtVg03Oam-TZB43kDTlMYYWpwbvFMIPYBfLOaxB1XiLImaDoj7Po_0RKCeP6VV-xhdrFyTdt4vPKxEsGh-hFq2yLFi5ROxlkS4CnK254IHVQhITUstjZrnnvWZ-sTMPJ5IdDxgaNtgGTTtg' alt='People on the streets of Havana during a nationwide blackout on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Aid arrivals: Humanitarian organizations began flying assistance into Cuba on March 21, including solar panels, food and medicine meant to ease the immediate strain from the blackout and broader shortages.</li><li>Havana scenes: Le Monde said Havana&#x27;s streets were pitch black after the grid failed, forcing people to get around with flashlights during the nighttime outage.</li><li>Official notice: Cuba&#x27;s Energy Ministry said on X that a &quot;total disconnection&quot; of the national electricity system had occurred and that crews had already started restoration work.</li><li>Monthly pattern: Reports described the new outage as Cuba&#x27;s third major blackout since March 4, underscoring how unstable the electricity system has become beyond this week&#x27;s two nationwide failures.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuba&#x27;s Energy Ministry: The ministry described the event as a complete separation of the national system and said power-restoration work began immediately after the collapse. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/cuba-announces-second-nationwide-blackout-in-less-than-a-week/article70771382.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Humanitarian organizations: CBS News said aid groups began air deliveries of solar panels, food and medicine to Cuba. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-second-nationwide-power-outage-march/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>International media reporting: Several outlets framed the blackout as part of a broader fuel and infrastructure crisis, tying the repeated failures to decaying power assets and restrictions on oil supplies reaching Cuba. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0l44yxrvo'>BBC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/cuban-power-grid-collapses-for-second-time-in-a-week-amid-us-oil-blockade'>Cuban power grid collapses for second time in a week amid US oil blockade</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/cuba-hit-by-second-island-wide-blackout-in-a-week/a-76471197'>Cuba hit by second island-wide blackout in a week</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0l44yxrvo'>National blackout hits Cuba for second time in a week</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/cuba-reports-nationwide-power-grid-outage-week-131293192'>Cuba reports second nationwide power grid outage in a week</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/22/cuba-hit-by-second-nationwide-blackout-in-a-week_6751687_4.html'>Cuba hit by second nationwide blackout in a week</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/wo